  "prefLabel": "We 204.01 Applicability",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "We 204.01 Applicability. Any interested person may petition the board to waive a procedural rule, or request a declaratory ruling on the applicability of any statute, rule, or order administered or enforced by the board, or may request an exemption of a rule or one or more of the provisions of RSA 482-B. The rules in this part shall apply to any petition to waive a rule, petition for declaratory ruling, or request for an exemption pursuant to RSA 482-B:13. Petitions for waiver shall apply to procedural rules of this chapter. Petitions for an exemption shall apply to the provisions of RSA 482-B and rules adopted by the board.\n\nSource. #7307, eff 6-13-00; ss by #9178-A, eff 6-13-08",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/we100-1000.html"
